	// Specifies IP ranges that are reserved and excluded from being assigned by the DHCP server to clients. These reserved IPs must not overlap with system-reserved addresses, including the gateway IP, network IP, DHCP server IP, and broadcast IP, and they must belong to the defined subnet CIDR. The reserved IPs can be provided as either a single IP address or an IP address range. Only IPv4 addresses are supported. Supported formats include: [\"192.168.1.1\", \"192.168.1.3-192.168.1.100\"]
